WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.101
-Good evening.

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:03.202
I'm Seth Meyers,
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:04.370
We hope you're all
doing well tonight.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:08.574
As for us,
things have taken a turn.

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:09.742
Let's get to the news.

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:11.611
President Biden
is set to deliver

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:14.547
his first State of the Union
address on March 1st,

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:19.218
and it's the first one where
"union" is the only good news.

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:20.819
Republican senator
Lindsey Graham yesterday

00:00:20.819 --> 00:00:22.454
criticized
President Biden's speech

00:00:22.454 --> 00:00:24.891
commemorating
the January 6th Capitol attack,

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:27.760
and said Biden had
"politicized the event."

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:32.098
How do you politicize an event
that's already political?

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:35.435
They stormed the Capitol,
not a Best Buy on Black Friday.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.303
That's like saying,
"Is it just me,

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:42.541
or is the priest's sermon today
all about religion?

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:45.311
We get it. We get it."

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.714
In a speech last week
commemorating

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.616
the one-year anniversary
of the Capitol attack,

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:52.318
President Biden criticized
the rioters and said,

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:55.187
"You can't love your country
only when you win."

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:57.023
Well, I guess some people

00:00:57.023 --> 00:01:00.659
are just never meant
to fall in love.

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:02.161
Advisors to
former President Trump

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.163
reportedly believe that
a recent improvement

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:05.732
in Trump's favorability rating

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:08.067
is due to his diminished
social media presence,

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:11.437
and at this point,
Biden will try anything.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:14.307
Scientists are currently
disputing a new study

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:16.709
that claims to have discovered
a so-called

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:19.712
"deltachron" strain
of the coronavirus

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.481
that combines
the delta and omicron variants,

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:27.219
and the only thing that can
stop it is the Pfizerna vaccine.

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:28.788
Scientists in England
recently announced

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.356
that they've named
a type of tree

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.692
after actor Leonardo DiCaprio,

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:35.861
and it's currently dating
a sapling.

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:38.464
A little tree humor,

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:40.700
for everybody out there
who's into that kind of thing.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.503
New York Mayor Eric Adams
is facing criticism

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:46.072
over his recent decision
to appoint his brother

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.441
to serve as
the deputy police commissioner.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:51.110
Said Adams,
"Cool. Take it up with my son."

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.879
I'm gonna say it right now --

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:57.116
I think this Mayor Adams thing
is off to a great start --

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:59.185
insofar as, you know,

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.653
monologue jokes.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:01.820
Hot start.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.722
Don't want to jinx it.

00:02:03.722 --> 00:02:05.658
Hot start.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.726
Mercedes-Benz recently unveiled

00:02:07.726 --> 00:02:11.998
its new
all-electric concept car,

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:14.500
which is made from
several sustainable materials,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.636
can travel 620 miles
on a single charge,

00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:21.574
and takes up two parking spots.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.943
BlackBerry last week officially
stopped supporting

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.145
its line of
signature mobile devices.

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:27.613
Of course,
I was totally prepared,

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:33.552
because I set a reminder
on my PalmPilot.

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:36.722
And finally, Taco Bell
announced its so-called

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:39.491
"Taco Lover's Pass"
subscription service last week,

00:02:39.491 --> 00:02:42.962
which costs $10 a month
to receive one taco per day

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.264
for 30 consecutive days.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.566
On the downside,
"Taco Lovers Pass"

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:50.636
will also be the headline
of their obituary.

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:55.074
Now that's the kind of joke
you can do, you know,

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.409
when you're
in an empty apartment.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.912
You don't have to worry
about the groans.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.145
Right?

00:03:00.145 --> 00:03:01.981
Tell the jokes you want to tell

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.215
about Taco Bell.

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:04.617
What do you mean,
who am I taking to?

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.052
Who are you talking to?

